IBG Connectivity – Operational Access Flow
	1.	Operations Team User Access
	•	The Operations team user logs in from their local workstation.
	2.	Access via PAM
	•	The user connects to the PAM (Privileged Access Management) system for secure privileged access.
	3.	Connection to Bot Runtime Machine
	•	From PAM, the user connects to the Bot Runtime Machine using Dameware remote access.
	4.	Runtime Machine Environment
	•	The Runtime Machine contains all required software and automation dependencies installed, such as:
	•	Blue Prism Runtime
	•	Required application clients
	•	Supporting utilities
	5.	Connection to Blue Prism Platform
	•	The Runtime Machine connects to:
	•	Blue Prism Application Server Load Balancer
	•	Blue Prism Hub Load Balancer
	6.	Automation Execution
	•	Bots run on the Runtime Machine and communicate with the Blue Prism environment through the load balancers.

